+## Subtopics
+
+### VQ-Based SH-AC Compression
+A method that independently quantizes the SH-AC vector of each Gaussian by mapping it to a VQ codevector, rather than exploiting spatial correlation between neighbors [S2]. Because VQ codevector selection does not use reconstructed values or spatial predictions of neighboring Gaussians, a codevector with differing color characteristics may be assigned to an individual Gaussian, causing localized color inconsistency [S2]. At RP2 on the Bartender dataset, the proposed method produces a bitstream size of 7.44 MB, which is smaller than the anchor's 9.60 MB [S2]. Unlike the anchor, the proposed method does not directly exploit spatial correlation among neighboring Gaussians, which can lead to localized color distortions inconsistent with surrounding tones [S2].
+
 ## Operating characteristics
